From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 14:18:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] spi: spidev: add commaai,panda compatible

The panda is comma's CAN interface microcontroller. On the comma four it
sits on an SPI bus of the SoC, and openpilot drives it from userspace
through spidev. Register the commaai,panda compatible in spidev, so that
the device tree can describe the panda and get a /dev/spidevB.C for it
without binding spidev by hand.

This is local to AGNOS: the compatible uses the old commaai prefix, which
upstream would not take next to comma.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/spi/spidev.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spidev.c b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
index 15d2aaeb08..87ec8cb8a8 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spidev.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
@@ -687,6 +687,7 @@ static const struct spi_device_id spidev_spi_ids[] = {
 	{ .name = /* abb */ "spi-sensor" },
 	{ .name = /* arduino */ "unoq-mcu" },
 	{ .name = /* cisco */ "spi-petra" },
+	{ .name = /* commaai */ "panda" },
 	{ .name = /* dh */ "dhcom-board" },
 	{ .name = /* elgin */ "jg10309-01" },
 	{ .name = /* gocontroll */ "moduline-module-slot"},
@@ -721,6 +722,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id spidev_dt_ids[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "abb,spi-sensor", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "arduino,unoq-mcu", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "cisco,spi-petra", .data = &spidev_of_check },
+	{ .compatible = "commaai,panda", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "dh,dhcom-board", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "elgin,jg10309-01", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "gocontroll,moduline-module-slot", .data = &spidev_of_check},
